From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:03:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 089/184] segacd: timeshare phase 2 in progress -- BIOS reads
 attempted, not yet working

The visit survives a full read attempt: DRV_INIT to wake firmware whose
internal state has been frozen since eviction, CDCSTOP, ROMREADN, and
the CDCSTAT/CDCREAD/CDCTRN/CDCACK loop, all with Sega's vectors in low
memory and the gate array passing levels 4 and 5 so its own handlers
drive the state machine. EmuTOS comes back intact every time and the
diagnostic runs on afterwards. What does not yet happen is a sector.

Fixed on the way, both mine: the interrupt mask was cleared with
0xFCFF, which leaves bit 10 set, so the following ori restored level 7
and Sega's handlers never ran at all; and the C wrapper collapsed every
failure to 1, discarding the only thing the read had to say.

Scratch for the visit -- stack, packet, buffer -- is 0x7C000-0x7EFFF,
taken off the top of the A: ramdisk. It has to be above phystop, where
EmuTOS never allocates, and outside the 24 KB that gets exchanged; that
region is the only memory on the machine that is both.

Current state: read returns 0x0FAA rather than a stage code, which does
not match any path in the routine, so the next step is finding out what
is clobbering d5 across the BIOS calls -- the documented clobber list
is d0-d1/a0-a1 and the real one is evidently wider.

Normal boots are unaffected: none of this runs outside the diagnostic.
